---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="AWS Architecture Journey | Built By Raza"
  description="Documenting my hands-on journey through AWS architecture, cloud networking and resilient infrastructure."
>

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">CLOUD · AWS</p>

      <h1>
        AWS Architecture Journey
      </h1>

      <p class="intro">
        Building cloud architecture skills by designing, testing and
        documenting real AWS environments.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">WHY I'M BUILDING THIS</p>
        <h2>Extending a networking foundation into cloud architecture.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="copy">
        <p>
          My background is in telecommunications, networking and solution
          architecture. AWS is the next layer I’m adding to that foundation.
        </p>

        <p>
          Rather than learning only for a certification exam, I want to build
          real environments, understand the design decisions behind them and
          document what happens when things work — and when they fail.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-label">PROJECT ROADMAP</p>
      <h2>What I plan to build.</h2>

      <div class="roadmap-grid">
        <article class="roadmap-card">
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Production-Style VPC</h3>
          <p>
            Public and private subnets, routing, Internet Gateway, NAT,
            security groups and multi-AZ design.
          </p>
          <a href="/projects/aws-vpc-lab">View Lab →</a>
        </article>

        <article class="roadmap-card">
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Highly Available Application</h3>
          <p>
            Load balancing, Auto Scaling, EC2 and resilient database design.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="roadmap-card">
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Multi-VPC Architecture</h3>
          <p>
            Production, development and shared-services VPCs connected
            through Transit Gateway.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="roadmap-card">
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Hybrid Cloud</h3>
          <p>
            Connecting enterprise infrastructure to AWS using VPN,
            Direct Connect concepts and BGP.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="roadmap-card">
          <span>05</span>
          <h3>Infrastructure as Code</h3>
          <p>
            Rebuilding AWS environments using Terraform and reusable modules.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="roadmap-card">
          <span>06</span>
          <h3>Cloud + AI Infrastructure</h3>
          <p>
            Exploring how cloud architecture connects to GPU workloads
            and modern AI infrastructure.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">HOW I'M LEARNING</p>
        <h2>Learn. Build. Break. Fix. Document.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="copy">
        <p>
          For each topic, I plan to build a working environment first,
          then deliberately test failure scenarios and routing behavior.
        </p>

        <p>
          Each completed lab will include architecture diagrams,
          design notes, lessons learned and eventually Terraform code
          in GitHub.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">CURRENT STATUS</p>
        <h2>In progress.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="status-box">
        <p>Current focus</p>
        <strong>AWS Solutions Architect – Associate</strong>

        <p>Next build</p>
        <strong>Production-Style AWS VPC</strong>

        <p>Documentation</p>
        <strong>Architecture diagrams + GitHub notes</strong>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding: 120px 0 105px;
  }

  .narrow {
    max-width: 900px;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .section-label {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: #6b7280;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 18px 0 24px;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5.7rem);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 8px 0 20px;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.2rem);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  h3 {
    margin: 14px 0 10px;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }

  .intro {
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: #4b5563;
  }

  .section {
    padding: 95px 0;
  }

  .alt {
    background: #f7f7f8;
  }

  .split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 80px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .copy p {
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 22px;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    color: #4b5563;
  }

  .roadmap-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 22px;
    margin-top: 45px;
  }

  .roadmap-card {
    padding: 28px;
    border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: #ffffff;
  }
  .roadmap-card a {
  display: inline-block;
  margin-top: 10px;
  color: #111827;
  font-weight: 750;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.roadmap-card a:hover {
  text-decoration: underline;
}

  .roadmap-card span {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: #9ca3af;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .roadmap-card p {
    color: #6b7280;
  }

  .status-box {
    padding: 30px;
    border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: white;
  }

  .status-box p {
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    color: #6b7280;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .status-box strong {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 22px;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 850px) {
    .split,
    .roadmap-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .split {
      gap: 24px;
    }
  }
</style>